{
  "tema": 5965,
  "slug": "para-destino-salgo-para",
  "titulo": "Para (not por) for a destination",
  "subtitulo": "«Salgo para Ensenada mañana.»",
  "foto": "t02.jpg",
  "regla": "To say where someone or something is headed, use para after verbs of movement (ir, salir, venir, partir) and with vehicles or things going somewhere. Por with a place means through or around, not to.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With verbs of movement, **para** marks the **destination**: where you are headed."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "ir / salir / venir / partir",
            "+ para +",
            "place"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "It also tells where a bus, a flight or a package **is going**: **el camión para Rosarito**, **un vuelo para Cancún**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Para** stresses the direction more than the arrival. With **ir** you can also use **a**: **voy a la playa** and **voy para la playa** both work; **para** sounds like _I'm on my way there_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Por** + place is something else: **through**, **along** or **around** (**salgo por Ensenada** = _I'm leaving via Ensenada_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **para** is the arrow on the map; it points to the end of the trip."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Mañana ==salgo para== Ensenada temprano.",
              "en": "Tomorrow I'm leaving for Ensenada early."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Este camión ==va para== Rosarito?",
              "en": "Does this bus go to Rosarito?"
            },
            {
              "es": "==Ya voy para== tu casa.",
              "en": "I'm on my way to your place now."
            },
            {
              "es": "Mis primos ==vienen para== Tijuana en diciembre.",
              "en": "My cousins are coming to Tijuana in December."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿A qué hora sale el vuelo ==para== Monterrey?",
              "en": "What time does the flight to Monterrey leave?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Después del trabajo ==nos vamos para== la playa.",
              "en": "After work we're heading to the beach."
            },
            {
              "es": "Este paquete ==va para== San Diego.",
              "en": "This package is going to San Diego."
            },
            {
              "es": "¡==Vente para== acá!",
              "en": "Come over here!"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Mañana salgo por Ensenada."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Mañana salgo para Ensenada."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "**Por** = via Ensenada; **para** = heading to Ensenada."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "¿Este camión va por Rosarito?"
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "¿Este camión va para Rosarito?"
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Ask for the destination with **para**."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Voy por la playa."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Voy para la playa."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "**Ir por** + thing or place usually means _go get_ or _go through_."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Salgo Ensenada mañana."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Salgo para Ensenada mañana."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "**Salir** needs a preposition before the place."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "parientes",
      "titulo": "Related rules",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "usos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "forma": "para + purpose",
              "texto": "The other basic **para**: [[5970|para for purpose]]."
            },
